    <tags>bff-api, background, scheduling, auth, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Owner decisions 2026-09-18/19. D-1 option B (plugins ruled out repo-wide, so the undated-grant repair needs a non-Dataverse mechanism), ISS-026/#1006 write half ("check statecode and deactivate if org is inactive"), and ISS-020/#999 part 4 (the deactivation writer). Consolidated into ONE task because all three need the identical mechanism; authoring three overlapping jobs is the duplication CLAUDE.md §11 forbids. Recorded in notes/owner-decision-brief-2026-09-18.md § "Nothing is blocked".</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Three separate defects share one root: a row's own columns are not the truth about whether it confers access, so something must re-derive it from a parent or a date on every read — and nothing ever does. Deactivating an organization revokes nothing. A membership ended by date keeps conferring. A grant created outside the BFF has no expiry, so it is both unbounded and invisible to the expiry reminders. Build ONE scheduled job that writes the row so its own statecode / sprk_expiresdate IS the answer.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer — the external-access evaluator, Dataverse writes, and the Spaarke.Scheduling framework. You are changing who has access to what; treat every write as an access-removal event.</role>

  <goal>One IScheduledJob in the BFF, registered through AddScheduledJob&lt;TJob&gt;, that applies three reconciliation rules idempotently with real paging and transactional chunked writes, ships DISABLED with a report-only mode, and records a before-state for every row it would change.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner ruled out Dataverse plugins repo-wide (D-1), which removed the only in-transaction mechanism task 107 had for stamping a default expiry. D-1's answer is A + B + C: A inverts the READ default (task 107, sibling), B is THIS job, C is the role/UI change (task 118). Separately ISS-026 found that NO query on the organization access path consults sprk_organization.statecode, so deactivating a firm is a silent no-op; and ISS-020 part 4 needs a writer for date-ended memberships because nothing in the repo writes the junction at all — those rows are maker-authored (verified: 13 hits for sprk_contactorganization under src/server are all reads, projections or comments).

⚠️ THE ENVIRONMENT IS DEV AND ITS RECORDS ARE TEST RECORDS (owner, 2026-09-17). That changes urgency, not validity — every rule here becomes an access-removal event the moment a real customer environment exists.

Verified facts you may rely on (each checked 2026-09-19 against source, not inherited from a comment):
- DataverseWebApiClient.QueryAsync&lt;T&gt; (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiClient.cs:227-246) issues ONE GET and returns result?.Value; its ODataCollectionResponse declares @odata.nextLink at :296-297 and NEVER READS IT. Its UpdateAsync (:204-214) is one PATCH per row with no transaction. So that client can serve neither an unbounded scan nor a batched write.
- IGenericEntityService.BulkUpdateAsync (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IGenericEntityService.cs:65) is ONE ExecuteTransactionRequest, all-or-nothing (task 096), and it CANNOT set a field to DBNull (DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:2397). That is fine here: every write sets a value, none clears one.
- Deactivation in this codebase writes BOTH fields together: ["statecode"]=1, ["statuscode"]=2 (Api/ExternalAccess/ProjectClosureEndpoint.cs:405-406). statecode alone leaves an inconsistent status reason.
- A NULL statecode counts as ACTIVE: ExternalGrantLifecycle.IsActive =&gt; StateCode is null or 0 (:121). The scan must treat null as active.
- The junction schema was live-verified by Dataverse MCP describe on 2026-08-26 and is recorded at Api/ExternalAccess/RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:659-665 — collection sprk_contactorganizations; lookups projected as _sprk_contact_value / _sprk_organization_value; statecode Active(0)/Inactive(1). There is NO entity-schema.md for sprk_contactorganization or sprk_organization (only 7 entities have one), so that comment is the best offline source.
- The server's default expiry already exists as a named constant: ExternalGrantLifecycle.DefaultExpiryDays = 90 (:160) with DefaultExpiry(DateOnly today) (:171) and TodayUtc(TimeProvider) (:167), from task 097's "server fills +90". REUSE IT. Do not write another 90.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessReconciliationJob.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ExternalAccess/GrantExpiryReminderJob.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipReconciliationJob.cs</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalGrantLifecycle.cs</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs</file>
