    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Scheduled job in the BFF" location=".claude/patterns/api/scheduled-jobs.md">Read these files first; mirror GrantExpiryReminderJob's ExecuteAsync skeleton (:157-234) exactly — one scope per run, one paged query, per-row try/catch that continues, ok/partial/error/cancelled status, a problems list, and ExceptionDispatchInfo rethrow ONLY when the run made no progress.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Discovery-driven Dataverse reconciliation" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipReconciliationJob.cs">The recon SHAPE to follow: scan parents paginated via IGenericEntityService with PagingInfo, honour the token between pages, count per-rule outcomes into ResultJson, and let one bad row log-and-continue. Note it reconciles a DIFFERENT junction (sprk_userentityassociation) against different sources — copy the shape, not the domain.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Re-verify live metadata before designing R3: sprk_enddate's type and behaviour, and whether sprk_startdate exists. The Dataverse MCP server was DOWN when this task was authored, so these are UNVERIFIED. If sprk_enddate is not Date-Only, fire the escalation below rather than choosing a comparison.</step>
    <step order="1">Measure the before-state with a report-only pass: how many rows each of R1, R2, R3 would change, and list them. This is the owner's D-2 part 3 precondition and it gates any write.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the job: paged reads via IGenericEntityService, the three rules, chunked BulkUpdateAsync writes with an atomic claim and completion marker per chunk, ResultJson per-rule breakdown, one heartbeat per attempt.</step>
    <step order="3">Register it in ExternalAccessModule beside GrantExpiryReminderJob via AddScheduledJob&lt;TJob&gt;, DISABLED, mirroring that call's ADR-032 unconditional-registration reasoning at :349-352.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests per the closed set below; perturbations; build, full suite, ArchTests, publish size vs a fresh master; notes; TASK-INDEX row.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>sprk_enddate's type/behaviour is UNVERIFIED (MCP was down at authoring). If it is DateTime/UserLocal rather than Date-Only, a read-time date comparison is the wrong instrument and rule R3 MUST NOT ship as specified — owner decision D-2 names exactly this as the thing that would change the answer. STOP and escalate; do not pick a comparison.</trigger>
    <trigger>If sprk_startdate exists, a not-yet-STARTED membership is a second fail direction this task never scoped. STOP and escalate rather than extending scope silently.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the Step 1 report shows R2 or R3 would deactivate more than a handful of rows, that is an access-removal event requiring owner sign-off before any write — not an implementation detail. STOP and report the counts and the list.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any row would need a field CLEARED rather than set, BulkUpdateAsync cannot express it (DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:2397). STOP rather than switching to per-row PATCH, which would silently drop the all-or-nothing guarantee.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Four neighbours, each checked: GrantExpiryReminderJob.cs (same module, same grant entity, daily paged scan — but it only READS and notifies, and its window is today..+30 so it cannot see an undated or a stale row); MembershipReconciliationJob.cs (the recon shape, but a different junction, sprk_userentityassociation, against different sources of truth); ExternalOrganizationMembership (RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:667-734, org to members) and ExternalParticipationService.QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync (contact to orgs, private, its own app-only token flow) — both org-scoped readers on DataverseWebApiClient.</existing>
    <extension>No, and the reason is mechanical rather than aesthetic: both junction readers sit on DataverseWebApiClient.QueryAsync, verified at :227-246 to issue one GET and never read the @odata.nextLink it declares at :296-297, with a 200-row bound (MaxMembersPerSweep); a reconciliation scan is unbounded by nature, so that client cannot serve it, and its UpdateAsync (:204-214) is one untransacted PATCH per row. GrantExpiryReminderJob has no write path and the wrong window. What IS reused rather than rebuilt: IGenericEntityService paging, BulkUpdateAsync, ExternalGrantLifecycle's date rule, IIdempotencyService, and the AddScheduledJob host.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Three concrete, named failures. (1) Deactivating an organization record — the obvious operator gesture for "this firm is no longer engaged" — is a silent no-op: its grant rows stay active, its membership rows stay active, and every member keeps inherited access to every record the firm held, with no error and no surface that shows it. (2) A membership ended by date keeps conferring access indefinitely, because nothing in the repo writes the junction; live org grants existed (notes/task-020-org-grant-spe-cleanup.md:18). (3) An externally-created grant row with no sprk_expiresdate is both unbounded AND invisible to task 100's reminders, which select only today..+30 — so it never expires and nobody is ever told it did not.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

